{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI ships ready-made middleware so you don't have to hand-roll the common cases. Each one is an ordinary "},{"type":"link","href":"./middleware","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — drop it into the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware"},{"type":"text","value":" array of any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. This page documents every built-in."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it does"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCacheMiddleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cache tool-call results by name + arguments"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contentGuardMiddleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Redact / transform / block streamed text content"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emit OpenTelemetry spans + GenAI metrics"}]}]]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCacheMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contentGuardMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" are exported from the main "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares"},{"type":"text","value":" barrel. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" lives on its own subpath ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel"},{"type":"text","value":") so that importing the barrel never eagerly pulls in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@opentelemetry/api"},{"type":"text","value":" (an optional peer dependency)."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For app-owned policies (for example tool-call budgets), see the "},{"type":"link","href":"../chat/agentic-cycle#tool-call-budgets-middleware-recipe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool-call budget recipe"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — those stay in your code, not in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"toolcachemiddleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"toolCacheMiddleware"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caches tool call results based on tool name and arguments. When a tool is called with the same name and arguments as a previous call, the cached result is returned immediately without re-executing the tool."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Identical calls in one model turn run at the same time, so both of them miss the cache. To let the second call use the first result, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolExecution: 'sequential'"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\nimport { weatherTool, stockTool } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What's the weather in Paris?\" }],\n  tools: [weatherTool, stockTool],\n  middleware: [\n    toolCacheMiddleware({\n      ttl: 60_000, // Cache entries expire after 60 seconds\n      maxSize: 50, // Keep at most 50 entries (LRU eviction)\n      toolNames: [\"getWeather\"], // Only cache specific tools\n    }),\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options:"}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"100"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maximum cache entries. Oldest evicted first (LRU). Only applies to the default in-memory storage."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ttl"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Infinity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Time-to-live in milliseconds. Expired entries are not served."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolNames"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All tools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only cache these tools. Others pass through."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyFn"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(toolName, args) => string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSON.stringify([toolName, args])"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom cache key derivation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"storage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolCacheStorage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In-memory Map"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom storage backend. When provided, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSize"},{"type":"text","value":" is ignored — the storage manages its own capacity."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behaviors:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only successful tool calls are cached — errors are never stored"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cache hits trigger "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'skip', result }"},{"type":"text","value":" via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeToolCall"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LRU eviction: when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSize"},{"type":"text","value":" is reached, the oldest entry is removed (default storage only)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cache hits refresh the entry's LRU position (moved to most-recently-used)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom key function"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — useful when you want to ignore certain arguments:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolCacheMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n\nfunction isRecord(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {\n  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null;\n}\n\ntoolCacheMiddleware({\n  keyFn: (toolName, args) => {\n    // Ignore pagination, cache by query only. `args` is `unknown`, so\n    // narrow it with a type guard before destructuring.\n    if (!isRecord(args)) return JSON.stringify([toolName, args]);\n    const { page, ...rest } = args;\n    return JSON.stringify([toolName, rest]);\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"custom-storage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Storage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default the cache lives in-memory and is scoped to a single "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCacheMiddleware()"},{"type":"text","value":" instance. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"storage"},{"type":"text","value":" option to use an external backend like Redis, localStorage, or a database. This also enables "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sharing a cache across multiple "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The storage interface:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ToolCacheEntry, type ToolCacheStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n\n// Implement this interface (exported from `@tanstack/ai/middlewares`):\ninterface MyStorage extends ToolCacheStorage {\n  getItem: (key: string) => ToolCacheEntry | undefined | Promise<ToolCacheEntry | undefined>;\n  setItem: (key: string, value: ToolCacheEntry) => void | Promise<void>;\n  deleteItem: (key: string) => void | Promise<void>;\n}\n\n// ToolCacheEntry is { result: unknown; timestamp: number }","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All methods may return a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":" for async backends. The middleware handles TTL checking — your storage just needs to store and retrieve entries."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Redis example:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createClient } from \"redis\";\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware, type ToolCacheStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\nimport { adapter, messages } from \"./server\";\nimport { weatherTool } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst redis = createClient();\n\nconst redisStorage: ToolCacheStorage = {\n  getItem: async (key) => {\n    const raw = await redis.get(`tool-cache:${key}`);\n    return raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : undefined;\n  },\n  setItem: async (key, value) => {\n    await redis.set(`tool-cache:${key}`, JSON.stringify(value));\n  },\n  deleteItem: async (key) => {\n    await redis.del(`tool-cache:${key}`);\n  },\n};\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages,\n  tools: [weatherTool],\n  middleware: [toolCacheMiddleware({ storage: redisStorage, ttl: 60_000 })],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sharing a cache across requests:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware, type ToolCacheStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\nimport { globalCache, app, adapter } from \"./server\";\nimport { weatherTool } from \"./tools\";\n\n// Create storage once, reuse across chat() calls\nconst sharedStorage: ToolCacheStorage = {\n  getItem: (key) => globalCache.get(key),\n  setItem: (key, value) => { globalCache.set(key, value); },\n  deleteItem: (key) => { globalCache.delete(key); },\n};\n\n// Both requests share the same cache\napp.post(\"/api/chat\", async (req: { body: { messages: unknown[] } }) => {\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter,\n    messages: req.body.messages,\n    tools: [weatherTool],\n    middleware: [toolCacheMiddleware({ storage: sharedStorage })],\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"contentguardmiddleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"contentGuardMiddleware"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filters or transforms streamed text content as it flows through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":". Use it to redact sensitive data (SSNs, emails, API keys), enforce a profanity filter, or rewrite text on the fly. Rules are applied to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT"},{"type":"text","value":" chunks; all other chunk types pass through untouched."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { contentGuardMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Tell me about customer 123-45-6789\" }],\n  middleware: [\n    contentGuardMiddleware({\n      rules: [\n        // Regex + replacement\n        { pattern: /\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, replacement: \"[SSN REDACTED]\" },\n        // Custom transform function\n        { fn: (text) => text.replaceAll(\"badword\", \"****\") },\n      ],\n      strategy: \"buffered\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options:"}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rules"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ContentGuardRule[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Applied in order; each rule receives the previous rule's output. A rule is either "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ pattern: RegExp; replacement: string }"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ fn: (text: string) => string }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'delta' | 'buffered'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'buffered'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How content is matched. See below."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bufferSize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"50"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(Buffered only) Characters held back before emitting, so patterns spanning chunk boundaries still match. Set it ≥ the longest pattern you expect. Flushed at stream end."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blockOnMatch"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", drop the entire chunk if any rule changes the content (instead of emitting the filtered version)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFiltered"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(info: ContentFilteredInfo) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callback fired whenever a rule changes content. Receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ messageId, original, filtered, strategy }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Matching strategies:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'buffered'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Accumulates content and applies rules to the settled portion, holding back a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bufferSize"},{"type":"text","value":" look-behind window so a pattern split across two chunks ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"...123-45\""},{"type":"text","value":" then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"-6789...\""},{"type":"text","value":") is still caught. The buffer is flushed when the message or run ends. Use this for anything that can span deltas — which is most redaction."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'delta'"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Applies rules to each delta in isolation as it arrives. Fastest and lowest-latency, but a pattern split across a chunk boundary may slip through. Use only when your patterns are guaranteed to fit within a single delta."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behaviors:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT"},{"type":"text","value":" chunks are inspected; every other chunk type passes through."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A rule that doesn't change the text is a no-op — the chunk passes through unchanged."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blockOnMatch: true"},{"type":"text","value":", a matched chunk is dropped entirely (returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":") rather than emitting the redacted text."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFiltered"},{"type":"text","value":" callback is for observability/audit — it fires with the before/after text but does not alter what is emitted."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"otelmiddleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"otelMiddleware"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emits vendor-neutral OpenTelemetry traces and metrics for every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call — a root span per call, a child span per agent-loop iteration, and a grandchild span per tool execution, all tagged with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/gen-ai/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GenAI semantic-convention attributes"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { otelMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel\";\nimport { trace, metrics } from \"@opentelemetry/api\";\nimport { messages } from \"./server\";\n\nconst otel = otelMiddleware({\n  tracer: trace.getTracer(\"my-app\"),\n  meter: metrics.getMeter(\"my-app\"), // optional — enables GenAI histograms\n});\n\nconst result = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [otel],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" has its own configuration surface (content capture, redaction, span-name formatting, attribute enrichment, lifecycle callbacks) and requires the optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@opentelemetry/api"},{"type":"text","value":" peer dependency. See the dedicated "},{"type":"link","href":"./otel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenTelemetry"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide for full setup, the span/metric catalogue, and all options."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"writing-your-own","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Writing your own"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These built-ins are just "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" objects — nothing about them is privileged. To build your own, see the "},{"type":"link","href":"./middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide for the full hook reference, the context object, and composition rules."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the full lifecycle and hook reference"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./otel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenTelemetry"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" in depth"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"toolcachemiddleware","text":"toolCacheMiddleware","level":2},{"id":"custom-storage","text":"Custom Storage","level":3},{"id":"contentguardmiddleware","text":"contentGuardMiddleware","level":2},{"id":"otelmiddleware","text":"otelMiddleware","level":2},{"id":"writing-your-own","text":"Writing your own","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack AI ships ready-made middleware so you don't have to hand-roll the common cases. Each one is an ordinary [`ChatMiddleware`](./middleware) — drop it into the `middleware` array of any `chat()` call. This page documents every built-in.\n\n| Middleware | Import | What it does |\n|------------|--------|--------------|\n| `toolCacheMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` | Cache tool-call results by name + arguments |\n| `contentGuardMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` | Redact / transform / block streamed text content |\n| `otelMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel` | Emit OpenTelemetry spans + GenAI metrics |\n\n> `toolCacheMiddleware` and `contentGuardMiddleware` are exported from the main `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` barrel. `otelMiddleware` lives on its own subpath (`@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel`) so that importing the barrel never eagerly pulls in `@opentelemetry/api` (an optional peer dependency).\n\nFor app-owned policies (for example tool-call budgets), see the [tool-call budget recipe](../chat/agentic-cycle#tool-call-budgets-middleware-recipe) — those stay in your code, not in `@tanstack/ai/middlewares`.\n\n## toolCacheMiddleware\n\nCaches tool call results based on tool name and arguments. When a tool is called with the same name and arguments as a previous call, the cached result is returned immediately without re-executing the tool.\n\nIdentical calls in one model turn run at the same time, so both of them miss the cache. To let the second call use the first result, set `toolExecution: 'sequential'` on `chat()`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\nimport { weatherTool, stockTool } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What's the weather in Paris?\" }],\n  tools: [weatherTool, stockTool],\n  middleware: [\n    toolCacheMiddleware({\n      ttl: 60_000, // Cache entries expire after 60 seconds\n      maxSize: 50, // Keep at most 50 entries (LRU eviction)\n      toolNames: [\"getWeather\"], // Only cache specific tools\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Options:**\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `maxSize` | `number` | `100` | Maximum cache entries. Oldest evicted first (LRU). Only applies to the default in-memory storage. |\n| `ttl` | `number` | `Infinity` | Time-to-live in milliseconds. Expired entries are not served. |\n| `toolNames` | `string[]` | All tools | Only cache these tools. Others pass through. |\n| `keyFn` | `(toolName, args) => string` | `JSON.stringify([toolName, args])` | Custom cache key derivation. |\n| `storage` | `ToolCacheStorage` | In-memory Map | Custom storage backend. When provided, `maxSize` is ignored — the storage manages its own capacity. |\n\n**Behaviors:**\n\n- Only successful tool calls are cached — errors are never stored\n- Cache hits trigger `{ type: 'skip', result }` via `onBeforeToolCall`\n- LRU eviction: when `maxSize` is reached, the oldest entry is removed (default storage only)\n- Cache hits refresh the entry's LRU position (moved to most-recently-used)\n\n**Custom key function** — useful when you want to ignore certain arguments:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n\nfunction isRecord(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {\n  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null;\n}\n\ntoolCacheMiddleware({\n  keyFn: (toolName, args) => {\n    // Ignore pagination, cache by query only. `args` is `unknown`, so\n    // narrow it with a type guard before destructuring.\n    if (!isRecord(args)) return JSON.stringify([toolName, args]);\n    const { page, ...rest } = args;\n    return JSON.stringify([toolName, rest]);\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Custom Storage\n\nBy default the cache lives in-memory and is scoped to a single `toolCacheMiddleware()` instance. Pass a `storage` option to use an external backend like Redis, localStorage, or a database. This also enables **sharing a cache across multiple `chat()` calls**.\n\nThe storage interface:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ToolCacheEntry, type ToolCacheStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n\n// Implement this interface (exported from `@tanstack/ai/middlewares`):\ninterface MyStorage extends ToolCacheStorage {\n  getItem: (key: string) => ToolCacheEntry | undefined | Promise<ToolCacheEntry | undefined>;\n  setItem: (key: string, value: ToolCacheEntry) => void | Promise<void>;\n  deleteItem: (key: string) => void | Promise<void>;\n}\n\n// ToolCacheEntry is { result: unknown; timestamp: number }\n```\n\nAll methods may return a `Promise` for async backends. The middleware handles TTL checking — your storage just needs to store and retrieve entries.\n\n**Redis example:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createClient } from \"redis\";\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware, type ToolCacheStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\nimport { adapter, messages } from \"./server\";\nimport { weatherTool } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst redis = createClient();\n\nconst redisStorage: ToolCacheStorage = {\n  getItem: async (key) => {\n    const raw = await redis.get(`tool-cache:${key}`);\n    return raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : undefined;\n  },\n  setItem: async (key, value) => {\n    await redis.set(`tool-cache:${key}`, JSON.stringify(value));\n  },\n  deleteItem: async (key) => {\n    await redis.del(`tool-cache:${key}`);\n  },\n};\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages,\n  tools: [weatherTool],\n  middleware: [toolCacheMiddleware({ storage: redisStorage, ttl: 60_000 })],\n});\n```\n\n**Sharing a cache across requests:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware, type ToolCacheStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\nimport { globalCache, app, adapter } from \"./server\";\nimport { weatherTool } from \"./tools\";\n\n// Create storage once, reuse across chat() calls\nconst sharedStorage: ToolCacheStorage = {\n  getItem: (key) => globalCache.get(key),\n  setItem: (key, value) => { globalCache.set(key, value); },\n  deleteItem: (key) => { globalCache.delete(key); },\n};\n\n// Both requests share the same cache\napp.post(\"/api/chat\", async (req: { body: { messages: unknown[] } }) => {\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter,\n    messages: req.body.messages,\n    tools: [weatherTool],\n    middleware: [toolCacheMiddleware({ storage: sharedStorage })],\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n});\n```\n\n## contentGuardMiddleware\n\nFilters or transforms streamed text content as it flows through `onChunk`. Use it to redact sensitive data (SSNs, emails, API keys), enforce a profanity filter, or rewrite text on the fly. Rules are applied to `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` chunks; all other chunk types pass through untouched.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { contentGuardMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Tell me about customer 123-45-6789\" }],\n  middleware: [\n    contentGuardMiddleware({\n      rules: [\n        // Regex + replacement\n        { pattern: /\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, replacement: \"[SSN REDACTED]\" },\n        // Custom transform function\n        { fn: (text) => text.replaceAll(\"badword\", \"****\") },\n      ],\n      strategy: \"buffered\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Options:**\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `rules` | `ContentGuardRule[]` | — | **Required.** Applied in order; each rule receives the previous rule's output. A rule is either `{ pattern: RegExp; replacement: string }` or `{ fn: (text: string) => string }`. |\n| `strategy` | `'delta' \\| 'buffered'` | `'buffered'` | How content is matched. See below. |\n| `bufferSize` | `number` | `50` | (Buffered only) Characters held back before emitting, so patterns spanning chunk boundaries still match. Set it ≥ the longest pattern you expect. Flushed at stream end. |\n| `blockOnMatch` | `boolean` | `false` | When `true`, drop the entire chunk if any rule changes the content (instead of emitting the filtered version). |\n| `onFiltered` | `(info: ContentFilteredInfo) => void` | — | Callback fired whenever a rule changes content. Receives `{ messageId, original, filtered, strategy }`. |\n\n**Matching strategies:**\n\n- **`'buffered'` (default)** — Accumulates content and applies rules to the settled portion, holding back a `bufferSize` look-behind window so a pattern split across two chunks (`\"...123-45\"` then `\"-6789...\"`) is still caught. The buffer is flushed when the message or run ends. Use this for anything that can span deltas — which is most redaction.\n- **`'delta'`** — Applies rules to each delta in isolation as it arrives. Fastest and lowest-latency, but a pattern split across a chunk boundary may slip through. Use only when your patterns are guaranteed to fit within a single delta.\n\n**Behaviors:**\n\n- Only `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` chunks are inspected; every other chunk type passes through.\n- A rule that doesn't change the text is a no-op — the chunk passes through unchanged.\n- With `blockOnMatch: true`, a matched chunk is dropped entirely (returns `null` from `onChunk`) rather than emitting the redacted text.\n- The `onFiltered` callback is for observability/audit — it fires with the before/after text but does not alter what is emitted.\n\n## otelMiddleware\n\nEmits vendor-neutral OpenTelemetry traces and metrics for every `chat()` call — a root span per call, a child span per agent-loop iteration, and a grandchild span per tool execution, all tagged with [GenAI semantic-convention attributes](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/gen-ai/).\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { otelMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel\";\nimport { trace, metrics } from \"@opentelemetry/api\";\nimport { messages } from \"./server\";\n\nconst otel = otelMiddleware({\n  tracer: trace.getTracer(\"my-app\"),\n  meter: metrics.getMeter(\"my-app\"), // optional — enables GenAI histograms\n});\n\nconst result = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [otel],\n});\n```\n\n`otelMiddleware` has its own configuration surface (content capture, redaction, span-name formatting, attribute enrichment, lifecycle callbacks) and requires the optional `@opentelemetry/api` peer dependency. See the dedicated [OpenTelemetry](./otel) guide for full setup, the span/metric catalogue, and all options.\n\n## Writing your own\n\nThese built-ins are just `ChatMiddleware` objects — nothing about them is privileged. To build your own, see the [Middleware](./middleware) guide for the full hook reference, the context object, and composition rules.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Middleware](./middleware) — the full lifecycle and hook reference\n- [OpenTelemetry](./otel) — `otelMiddleware` in depth","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Built-in Middleware\nid: built-in-middleware\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Ready-made TanStack AI chat() middleware — toolCacheMiddleware for caching tool results, contentGuardMiddleware for redacting streamed text, and otelMiddleware for OpenTelemetry tracing.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - middleware\n  - built-in middleware\n  - tool cache\n  - content guard\n  - redaction\n  - opentelemetry\n---\n\nTanStack AI ships ready-made middleware so you don't have to hand-roll the common cases. Each one is an ordinary [`ChatMiddleware`](./middleware) — drop it into the `middleware` array of any `chat()` call. This page documents every built-in.\n\n| Middleware | Import | What it does |\n|------------|--------|--------------|\n| `toolCacheMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` | Cache tool-call results by name + arguments |\n| `contentGuardMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` | Redact / transform / block streamed text content |\n| `otelMiddleware` | `@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel` | Emit OpenTelemetry spans + GenAI metrics |\n\n> `toolCacheMiddleware` and `contentGuardMiddleware` are exported from the main `@tanstack/ai/middlewares` barrel. `otelMiddleware` lives on its own subpath (`@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel`) so that importing the barrel never eagerly pulls in `@opentelemetry/api` (an optional peer dependency).\n\nFor app-owned policies (for example tool-call budgets), see the [tool-call budget recipe](../chat/agentic-cycle#tool-call-budgets-middleware-recipe) — those stay in your code, not in `@tanstack/ai/middlewares`.\n\n## toolCacheMiddleware\n\nCaches tool call results based on tool name and arguments. When a tool is called with the same name and arguments as a previous call, the cached result is returned immediately without re-executing the tool.\n\nIdentical calls in one model turn run at the same time, so both of them miss the cache. To let the second call use the first result, set `toolExecution: 'sequential'` on `chat()`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\nimport { weatherTool, stockTool } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What's the weather in Paris?\" }],\n  tools: [weatherTool, stockTool],\n  middleware: [\n    toolCacheMiddleware({\n      ttl: 60_000, // Cache entries expire after 60 seconds\n      maxSize: 50, // Keep at most 50 entries (LRU eviction)\n      toolNames: [\"getWeather\"], // Only cache specific tools\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Options:**\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `maxSize` | `number` | `100` | Maximum cache entries. Oldest evicted first (LRU). Only applies to the default in-memory storage. |\n| `ttl` | `number` | `Infinity` | Time-to-live in milliseconds. Expired entries are not served. |\n| `toolNames` | `string[]` | All tools | Only cache these tools. Others pass through. |\n| `keyFn` | `(toolName, args) => string` | `JSON.stringify([toolName, args])` | Custom cache key derivation. |\n| `storage` | `ToolCacheStorage` | In-memory Map | Custom storage backend. When provided, `maxSize` is ignored — the storage manages its own capacity. |\n\n**Behaviors:**\n\n- Only successful tool calls are cached — errors are never stored\n- Cache hits trigger `{ type: 'skip', result }` via `onBeforeToolCall`\n- LRU eviction: when `maxSize` is reached, the oldest entry is removed (default storage only)\n- Cache hits refresh the entry's LRU position (moved to most-recently-used)\n\n**Custom key function** — useful when you want to ignore certain arguments:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n\nfunction isRecord(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {\n  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null;\n}\n\ntoolCacheMiddleware({\n  keyFn: (toolName, args) => {\n    // Ignore pagination, cache by query only. `args` is `unknown`, so\n    // narrow it with a type guard before destructuring.\n    if (!isRecord(args)) return JSON.stringify([toolName, args]);\n    const { page, ...rest } = args;\n    return JSON.stringify([toolName, rest]);\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Custom Storage\n\nBy default the cache lives in-memory and is scoped to a single `toolCacheMiddleware()` instance. Pass a `storage` option to use an external backend like Redis, localStorage, or a database. This also enables **sharing a cache across multiple `chat()` calls**.\n\nThe storage interface:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type ToolCacheEntry, type ToolCacheStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n\n// Implement this interface (exported from `@tanstack/ai/middlewares`):\ninterface MyStorage extends ToolCacheStorage {\n  getItem: (key: string) => ToolCacheEntry | undefined | Promise<ToolCacheEntry | undefined>;\n  setItem: (key: string, value: ToolCacheEntry) => void | Promise<void>;\n  deleteItem: (key: string) => void | Promise<void>;\n}\n\n// ToolCacheEntry is { result: unknown; timestamp: number }\n```\n\nAll methods may return a `Promise` for async backends. The middleware handles TTL checking — your storage just needs to store and retrieve entries.\n\n**Redis example:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createClient } from \"redis\";\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware, type ToolCacheStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\nimport { adapter, messages } from \"./server\";\nimport { weatherTool } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst redis = createClient();\n\nconst redisStorage: ToolCacheStorage = {\n  getItem: async (key) => {\n    const raw = await redis.get(`tool-cache:${key}`);\n    return raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : undefined;\n  },\n  setItem: async (key, value) => {\n    await redis.set(`tool-cache:${key}`, JSON.stringify(value));\n  },\n  deleteItem: async (key) => {\n    await redis.del(`tool-cache:${key}`);\n  },\n};\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages,\n  tools: [weatherTool],\n  middleware: [toolCacheMiddleware({ storage: redisStorage, ttl: 60_000 })],\n});\n```\n\n**Sharing a cache across requests:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { toolCacheMiddleware, type ToolCacheStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\nimport { globalCache, app, adapter } from \"./server\";\nimport { weatherTool } from \"./tools\";\n\n// Create storage once, reuse across chat() calls\nconst sharedStorage: ToolCacheStorage = {\n  getItem: (key) => globalCache.get(key),\n  setItem: (key, value) => { globalCache.set(key, value); },\n  deleteItem: (key) => { globalCache.delete(key); },\n};\n\n// Both requests share the same cache\napp.post(\"/api/chat\", async (req: { body: { messages: unknown[] } }) => {\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter,\n    messages: req.body.messages,\n    tools: [weatherTool],\n    middleware: [toolCacheMiddleware({ storage: sharedStorage })],\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n});\n```\n\n## contentGuardMiddleware\n\nFilters or transforms streamed text content as it flows through `onChunk`. Use it to redact sensitive data (SSNs, emails, API keys), enforce a profanity filter, or rewrite text on the fly. Rules are applied to `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` chunks; all other chunk types pass through untouched.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { contentGuardMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Tell me about customer 123-45-6789\" }],\n  middleware: [\n    contentGuardMiddleware({\n      rules: [\n        // Regex + replacement\n        { pattern: /\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, replacement: \"[SSN REDACTED]\" },\n        // Custom transform function\n        { fn: (text) => text.replaceAll(\"badword\", \"****\") },\n      ],\n      strategy: \"buffered\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Options:**\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `rules` | `ContentGuardRule[]` | — | **Required.** Applied in order; each rule receives the previous rule's output. A rule is either `{ pattern: RegExp; replacement: string }` or `{ fn: (text: string) => string }`. |\n| `strategy` | `'delta' \\| 'buffered'` | `'buffered'` | How content is matched. See below. |\n| `bufferSize` | `number` | `50` | (Buffered only) Characters held back before emitting, so patterns spanning chunk boundaries still match. Set it ≥ the longest pattern you expect. Flushed at stream end. |\n| `blockOnMatch` | `boolean` | `false` | When `true`, drop the entire chunk if any rule changes the content (instead of emitting the filtered version). |\n| `onFiltered` | `(info: ContentFilteredInfo) => void` | — | Callback fired whenever a rule changes content. Receives `{ messageId, original, filtered, strategy }`. |\n\n**Matching strategies:**\n\n- **`'buffered'` (default)** — Accumulates content and applies rules to the settled portion, holding back a `bufferSize` look-behind window so a pattern split across two chunks (`\"...123-45\"` then `\"-6789...\"`) is still caught. The buffer is flushed when the message or run ends. Use this for anything that can span deltas — which is most redaction.\n- **`'delta'`** — Applies rules to each delta in isolation as it arrives. Fastest and lowest-latency, but a pattern split across a chunk boundary may slip through. Use only when your patterns are guaranteed to fit within a single delta.\n\n**Behaviors:**\n\n- Only `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` chunks are inspected; every other chunk type passes through.\n- A rule that doesn't change the text is a no-op — the chunk passes through unchanged.\n- With `blockOnMatch: true`, a matched chunk is dropped entirely (returns `null` from `onChunk`) rather than emitting the redacted text.\n- The `onFiltered` callback is for observability/audit — it fires with the before/after text but does not alter what is emitted.\n\n## otelMiddleware\n\nEmits vendor-neutral OpenTelemetry traces and metrics for every `chat()` call — a root span per call, a child span per agent-loop iteration, and a grandchild span per tool execution, all tagged with [GenAI semantic-convention attributes](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/gen-ai/).\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { otelMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel\";\nimport { trace, metrics } from \"@opentelemetry/api\";\nimport { messages } from \"./server\";\n\nconst otel = otelMiddleware({\n  tracer: trace.getTracer(\"my-app\"),\n  meter: metrics.getMeter(\"my-app\"), // optional — enables GenAI histograms\n});\n\nconst result = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [otel],\n});\n```\n\n`otelMiddleware` has its own configuration surface (content capture, redaction, span-name formatting, attribute enrichment, lifecycle callbacks) and requires the optional `@opentelemetry/api` peer dependency. See the dedicated [OpenTelemetry](./otel) guide for full setup, the span/metric catalogue, and all options.\n\n## Writing your own\n\nThese built-ins are just `ChatMiddleware` objects — nothing about them is privileged. To build your own, see the [Middleware](./middleware) guide for the full hook reference, the context object, and composition rules.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Middleware](./middleware) — the full lifecycle and hook reference\n- [OpenTelemetry](./otel) — `otelMiddleware` in depth"}
